    "result_text": "All green. Let me give a quick summary of the implementation.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the household membership-level ceiling: a new owner's `membershipLevel` is capped at one above the current maximum level among their existing household members, with no cap when the household has no existing members.\n\n**Where each piece lives (single responsibility, reusing existing patterns):**\n\n1. **`MembershipLevel`** (util) \u2014 now the single source of truth for an owner's *effective* level: `of(owner, asOf)` applies the owner's stored ceiling via a small private `capped(...)` helper. Both the DTO mapper and the audit log go through it, so they stay consistent.\n\n2. **`Owner`** + all four schema files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added a nullable `membershipLevelCap` / `membership_level_cap` column, mirroring how `householdSize` etc. are stored. The test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema column was required.\n\n3. **`Households`** (existing household helper) \u2014 added `maxMemberLevel(...)` returning `OptionalInt`, alongside the existing `memberCount(...)`. Empty result \u21d2 no existing members \u21d2 no cap.\n\n4. **`AssignMembershipLevelCap`** (new pipeline function) \u2014 computes and stamps the cap (`max + 1`) on the built owner, or leaves it unset when the household is empty. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `assignHousehold` (needs the `householdId`) and before `save`, under `transaction` governance like its neighbours.\n\n5. **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 the cap feature presupposes multi-member households (\"their household members\"), but this hard-blocked *any* second household member with a 409, which also made `AssignPossibleDuplicate`'s documented \"same household, different telephone \u2192 create + flag\" path dead code. Narrowed it to reject only an exact re-registration (same household **and** same telephone), which is precisely the \"same person\" definition `AssignPossibleDuplicate` already uses. A genuine duplicate (identical POST) still returns 409; distinct people in a household are now created and soft-flagged.\n\nThe audit log from the run confirms it: two same-household owners created \u2014 id 11 \u2192 level 1, id 12 \u2192 level 2 (capped at 1+1). Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1/1 tests passing.",
